Object.assign(window.AFYA_SWDICT,{"1 hour": "saa 1", "1 · Request": "1 · Ombi", "14 buyers listed": "Wanunuzi 14 wameorodheshwa", "2 · Pharmacist": "2 · Mfamasia", "3 · Sale": "3 · Mauzo", "302 days": "siku 302", "31–90 · front of shelf": "31–90 · mbele ya rafu", "39 days": "siku 39", "4 · Sealed bag": "4 · Mfuko uliofungwa", "80 days": "siku 80", "A recall in seven steps · and the worked example on one day": "Urejeshaji wa bidhaa kwa hatua saba · na mfano wa hesabu wa siku moja", "A torn or damp sterile pack is never sold": "Pakiti tasa iliyochanika au yenye unyevu kamwe haiuzwi", "Afya never chooses, opens, sells or takes payment for a medicine": "Afya kamwe haichagui, haifungui, haiuzi wala haipokei malipo ya dawa", "All 14 contacted": "Wote 14 wamewasiliana nao", "Batch number": "Namba ya toleo", "Budget TSh 6,000,000 a year": "Bajeti TSh 6,000,000 kwa mwaka", "Calls, checks the prescription": "Hupiga simu, hukagua cheti cha daktari", "Cause reviewed with the supplier": "Chanzo hupitiwa na msambazaji", "Certifies cosmetics, skin care, nappies and similar products before they are stocked.": "Huthibitisha vipodozi, bidhaa za utunzaji wa ngozi, nepi na bidhaa zinazofanana kabla ya kuwekwa dukani.", "Class II alert arrives": "Taarifa ya Daraja II inawasili", "Collect, refund or replace": "Kusanya, rejesha fedha au badilisha", "Concept image · a device with its written warranty": "Picha ya dhana · kifaa pamoja na dhamana yake ya maandishi", "Concept image · the stockroom, every shelf labelled by batch": "Picha ya dhana · stoo, kila rafu ikiwa na lebo ya toleo", "Enough shelf life left; oldest batch sold first": "Muda wa kutosha wa matumizi; toleo la zamani zaidi huuzwa kwanza", "Every hire": "Kila anayeajiriwa", "Every month · VAT and payroll returns, temperature and complaint logs reviewed": "Kila mwezi · ritani za VAT na mishahara, kumbukumbu za joto na malalamiko hupitiwa", "Every quarter · mock recall, offline-till test, expiry review of stock due within 90 days": "Kila robo mwaka · zoezi la kurejesha bidhaa, jaribio la kaunta bila mtandao, mapitio ya bidhaa zinazoisha muda ndani ya siku 90", "Expiry date": "Tarehe ya mwisho wa matumizi", "Five checks on every pack before it reaches a shelf": "Ukaguzi mara tano kwa kila pakiti kabla haijafika kwenye rafu", "Four batches of test strips on 1 November 2026 · days left before expiry": "Matoleo manne ya vipande vya vipimo tarehe 1 Novemba 2026 · siku zilizobaki kabla ya kwisha muda", "How one medicine order works · two businesses, one delivery": "Jinsi oda moja ya dawa inavyoshughulikiwa · biashara mbili, usafirishaji mmoja", "June · TMDA device permit renewed before 30 June; partner pharmacy licences filed": "Juni · kibali cha vifaa cha TMDA huhuishwa kabla ya 30 Juni; leseni za duka la dawa mshirika huhifadhiwa", "Kiswahili or English, maker’s name and address, sterility stated": "Kiswahili au Kiingereza, jina na anwani ya mtengenezaji, utasa umeelezwa", "Known fees against the yearly licence and insurance budget": "Ada zinazojulikana dhidi ya bajeti ya mwaka ya leseni na bima", "Label": "Lebo", "Labelled with the member’s name": "Ina lebo yenye jina la mwanachama", "Licenses the partner pharmacy and its pharmacist. Afya sells no medicines, so the store itself needs no pharmacy licence.": "Hutoa leseni kwa duka la dawa mshirika na mfamasia wake. Afya haiuzi dawa, hivyo duka lenyewe halihitaji leseni ya duka la dawa.", "Member asks in the app": "Mwanachama huomba kupitia programu", "Nine packs genuine and in standard, one substandard or falsified. A customer looking at the shelf cannot tell which.": "Pakiti tisa ni halisi na za kiwango, moja ni duni au bandia. Mteja anayeangalia rafu hawezi kujua ni ipi.", "On TMDA’s register or TBS-certified, or the exemption recorded": "Imo kwenye rejista ya TMDA au ina uthibitisho wa TBS, au msamaha umerekodiwa", "One medical product in ten · WHO estimate for low- and middle-income countries": "Bidhaa moja kati ya kumi za matibabu · makadirio ya WHO kwa nchi za kipato cha chini na cha kati", "Pack integrity": "Uimara wa pakiti", "Pharmacy receipt, paid directly": "Risiti ya duka la dawa, hulipwa moja kwa moja", "Published fees about TSh 80,000 a year (TMDA permit TSh 60,000; PDPC TSh 100,000 over five years)": "Ada zilizochapishwa takriban TSh 80,000 kwa mwaka (kibali cha TMDA TSh 60,000; PDPC TSh 100,000 kwa miaka mitano)", "Registers Afya as a data controller; Afya Check readings are sensitive data that need consent.": "Husajili Afya kama mdhibiti wa taarifa; vipimo vya Afya Check ni taarifa nyeti zinazohitaji ridhaa.", "Registers every device Afya sells, licenses the store for devices, receives safety reports, manages recalls.": "Husajili kila kifaa ambacho Afya huuza, hutoa leseni kwa duka kwa ajili ya vifaa, hupokea taarifa za usalama, husimamia urejeshaji wa bidhaa.", "Registration": "Usajili", "Replacements delivered": "Bidhaa mbadala zimefikishwa", "Rider carries it with the box": "Dereva wa pikipiki huubeba pamoja na boksi", "SMS, WhatsApp, phone, same day": "SMS, WhatsApp, simu, siku hiyohiyo", "Scanned and linked to the supplier and the delivery": "Huskaniwa na kuunganishwa na msambazaji na mzigo husika", "TMDA deadlines: Class I within 14 days, Class II within 21, Class III within 30 · Afya target: every affected customer contacted the same day": "Muda wa mwisho wa TMDA: Daraja I ndani ya siku 14, Daraja II ndani ya 21, Daraja III ndani ya 30 · Lengo la Afya: kila mteja aliyeathirika huwasiliana naye siku hiyohiyo", "TMDA or the maker notifies a batch": "TMDA au mtengenezaji hutoa taarifa ya toleo", "The compliance year · what falls due, month by month": "Mwaka wa uzingatiaji wa sheria · kinachopaswa kufanyika, mwezi kwa mwezi", "The rest covers insurance and the fees set at inspection (OSHA, fire, business licence)": "Kiasi kilichobaki kinagharamia bima na ada zinazowekwa wakati wa ukaguzi (OSHA, zimamoto, leseni ya biashara)", "The system lists every buyer": "Mfumo huorodhesha kila mnunuzi", "The system picks the batch that expires first, never simply the oldest delivery": "Mfumo huchagua toleo linaloisha muda kwanza, si tu mzigo wa zamani zaidi", "The till refuses the batch barcode": "Kaunta ya malipo hukataa msimbo pau wa toleo", "Till blocks the batch": "Kaunta inazuia toleo", "To TMDA; stock quarantined": "Kwa TMDA; bidhaa zimetengwa", "Yearly on set dates · business licence, OSHA licence, fire certificate · every 5 years · PDPC registration": "Kila mwaka kwa tarehe maalum · leseni ya biashara, leseni ya OSHA, cheti cha zimamoto · kila baada ya miaka 5 · usajili wa PDPC", "complaints acknowledged within 5 minutes": "malalamiko hupokelewa ndani ya dakika 5", "complaints closed within 5 days, with the customer’s agreement": "malalamiko hufungwa ndani ya siku 5, kwa ridhaa ya mteja", "contact with every affected customer when a recall arrives": "mawasiliano na kila mteja aliyeathirika urejeshaji unapotokea", "deliveries checked for batch and expiry on arrival": "mizigo hukaguliwa toleo na tarehe ya mwisho wa matumizi inapowasili", "expired or recalled units sold": "bidhaa zilizokwisha muda au zilizorejeshwa zilizouzwa", "faulty-on-arrival swap, in store or at the door": "kubadilisha kifaa chenye hitilafu kinapowasili, dukani au mlangoni", "monitor accuracy check at the Afya Check, any time": "ukaguzi wa usahihi wa kipimo kwenye Afya Check, wakati wowote", "over 90 days · sold normally and in monthly boxes": "zaidi ya siku 90 · huuzwa kawaida na kwenye maboksi ya kila mwezi", "regulators covered: TMDA, the Pharmacy Council, TBS and the PDPC": "wadhibiti wanaozingatiwa: TMDA, Baraza la Famasi, TBS na PDPC", "rentals cleaned, inspected and photographed": "vifaa vya kukodisha husafishwa, hukaguliwa na kupigwa picha", "return rules shown at the counter and in the app": "kanuni za urejeshaji zinaonyeshwa kaunta na kwenye programu", "temperature or humidity alarms left unreviewed after 24 hours": "ving’ora vya joto au unyevu visivyopitiwa baada ya saa 24", "to list every affected customer in a mock recall": "kuorodhesha kila mteja aliyeathirika katika zoezi la kurejesha bidhaa", "≤ 30 days · pulled": "≤ siku 30 · huondolewa"});

/* v111 Part 5 */
Object.assign(window.AFYA_SWDICT,{"(TSh 80,500 − TSh 8,500 packing and delivery) ÷ 1.153": "(TSh 80,500 − TSh 8,500 za kufungasha na kusafirisha) ÷ 1.153", ", and the national scheme started on 26 January 2026 at TSh 150,000 a year for a household of up to six": ", na mpango wa kitaifa ulianza tarehe 26 Januari 2026 kwa TSh 150,000 kwa mwaka kwa kaya ya hadi watu sita", ". At TSh 2,640 to the dollar, that is TSh 2,376 to TSh 6,336 per 1,000 views. If about half of the digital budget, TSh 375,000, goes on paid social posts, it buys roughly 59,186 to 157,828 views a month in the store’s neighbourhood. The other half pays for WhatsApp business messages to people who have opted in, which are reminders and invitations rather than advertising.": ". Kwa TSh 2,640 kwa dola moja, hiyo ni TSh 2,376 hadi TSh 6,336 kwa kila mara 1,000 za kutazamwa. Iwapo takriban nusu ya bajeti ya kidijitali, TSh 375,000, itatumika kwa machapisho ya kulipia kwenye mitandao ya kijamii, inanunua takriban mara 59,186 hadi 157,828 za kutazamwa kwa mwezi katika mtaa unaozunguka duka. Nusu nyingine inalipia ujumbe wa WhatsApp ya biashara kwa watu waliokubali kupokea, ambao ni vikumbusho na mialiko badala ya matangazo.", ". Employers and insurers are now looking for ways to keep people healthy at lower cost.": ". Waajiri na makampuni ya bima sasa wanatafuta njia za kuwaweka watu katika afya njema kwa gharama ndogo zaidi.", ". Employers and insurers now have a direct interest in keeping people healthy at lower cost, which is exactly what a monthly box, a free check and an employer first-aid service provide.": ". Waajiri na makampuni ya bima sasa wana maslahi ya moja kwa moja katika kuwaweka watu katika afya njema kwa gharama ndogo zaidi, na hicho ndicho hasa boksi la kila mwezi, kipimo cha bure na huduma ya huduma ya kwanza kwa waajiri vinavyotoa.", ". Its growth was financed by private equity together with development-finance lenders such as IFC and Proparco": ". Ukuaji wake ulifadhiliwa na mfuko wa uwekezaji binafsi pamoja na wakopeshaji wa fedha za maendeleo kama IFC na Proparco", ". Most are built for an acute need, such as a fever or a cough, not for the long-term care a family manages at home: the monthly test strips, nappies in the next size, a parent’s mobility aids. Afya Basics does not try to be the cheapest drug shop or the biggest supermarket. It competes on four things together: products that are provably registered, one published price in every channel, advice from trained advisers, and a plan that brings the household’s supplies before they run out.": ". Mengi yamejengwa kwa ajili ya mahitaji ya dharura, kama homa au kikohozi, si kwa huduma ya muda mrefu ambayo familia huisimamia nyumbani: vipande vya vipimo vya kila mwezi, nepi za ukubwa unaofuata, vifaa vya kusaidia kutembea vya mzazi. Afya Basics haijaribu kuwa duka la dawa la bei nafuu zaidi wala supamaketi kubwa zaidi. Inashindana kwa mambo manne kwa pamoja: bidhaa ambazo usajili wake unathibitishika, bei moja iliyotangazwa katika kila njia ya mauzo, ushauri kutoka kwa washauri waliofunzwa, na mpango unaoleta mahitaji ya kaya kabla hayajaisha.", ". The national scheme, “Bima ya Afya kwa Wote”, started on 26 January 2026 at TSh 150,000 a year for a household of up to six": ". Mpango wa kitaifa, “Bima ya Afya kwa Wote”, ulianza tarehe 26 Januari 2026 kwa TSh 150,000 kwa mwaka kwa kaya ya hadi watu sita", "02 · In summary · how customers are won and kept": "02 · Kwa muhtasari · jinsi wateja wanavyopatikana na kubakizwa", "02 · In summary · how one store becomes a chain": "02 · Kwa muhtasari · jinsi duka moja linavyokuwa mtandao wa maduka", "02 · In summary · where Afya Basics competes": "02 · Kwa muhtasari · mahali ambapo Afya Basics inashindana", "02 · In summary · why partners matter": "02 · Kwa muhtasari · kwa nini washirika ni muhimu", "03 · The economics of one store": "03 · Uchumi wa duka moja", "04 · How the chain is funded": "04 · Jinsi mtandao wa maduka unavyofadhiliwa", "05 · If customers buy less · how the gates limit the loss": "05 · Iwapo wateja watanunua kidogo · jinsi vizingiti vinavyopunguza hasara", "06 · What the marketing money buys": "06 · Fedha za masoko zinanunua nini", "07 · How business revenue is counted, with a worked example": "07 · Jinsi mapato ya biashara kwa taasisi yanavyohesabiwa, pamoja na mfano wa hesabu", "08 · Proof from the region · a health chain that scaled": "08 · Ushahidi kutoka kanda · mtandao wa maduka ya afya uliokua", "1 ÷ 8.0% of members leaving each month": "1 ÷ 8.0% ya wanachama wanaoondoka kila mwezi", "1.7 years": "miaka 1.7", "11 · The numbers · what a member costs and what a member is worth": "11 · Takwimu · gharama ya mwanachama na thamani yake", "12.5 months": "miezi 12.5", "2.9 months": "miezi 2.9", "A chain that opens stores faster than its existing stores earn will need outside capital until the earnings of the mature stores pay for the new ones. The chart shows the chain’s cumulative cash before tax, interest and working capital: the sum of each year’s EBITDA minus the capital spent on new stores.": "Mtandao wa maduka unaofungua maduka kwa kasi zaidi kuliko mapato ya maduka yaliyopo utahitaji mtaji kutoka nje hadi mapato ya maduka yaliyokomaa yaweze kulipia maduka mapya. Chati inaonyesha fedha taslimu limbikizi za mtandao kabla ya kodi, riba na mtaji wa uendeshaji: jumla ya EBITDA ya kila mwaka ukitoa mtaji uliotumika kwa maduka mapya.", "A clinic, an employer, a school, a hotel, an insurer or a diaspora association each serves many households at once. One agreement with one of them can bring Afya Basics dozens or hundreds of families without spending more on advertising.": "Kliniki, mwajiri, shule, hoteli, kampuni ya bima au jumuiya ya diaspora kila moja huhudumia kaya nyingi kwa wakati mmoja. Makubaliano moja na mmoja wao yanaweza kuiletea Afya Basics familia kadhaa au mamia bila kuongeza matumizi ya matangazo.", "Afya Basics (target)": "Afya Basics (lengo)", "Afya Basics does not buy its customers with discounts. It earns them with a free health check that people can see from the street, converts them with honest advice, and keeps them with a monthly Afya Box that renews itself. Marketing money therefore builds recurring revenue instead of one-off traffic.": "Afya Basics haiwanunui wateja wake kwa punguzo la bei. Inawapata kwa kipimo cha afya cha bure ambacho watu wanaweza kukiona wakiwa barabarani, inawageuza kuwa wateja kwa ushauri wa kweli, na inawabakiza kwa Afya Box ya kila mwezi inayojihuisha yenyewe. Kwa hiyo fedha za masoko hujenga mapato yanayojirudia badala ya wateja wa mara moja.", "Afya Basics store or same-day delivery": "Duka la Afya Basics au usafirishaji wa siku hiyohiyo", "Afya Box members at the end of month 12, base case": "Wanachama wa Afya Box mwishoni mwa mwezi wa 12, hali ya msingi", "Afya Checks · 1,815": "Vipimo vya Afya Check · 1,815", "Afya product families, 4–5 brands each": "Familia za bidhaa za Afya, chapa 4–5 kila moja", "All major Tanzanian cities": "Miji yote mikubwa ya Tanzania", "All members who joined, including those replacing members who left": "Wanachama wote waliojiunga, wakiwemo wanaochukua nafasi ya wanachama walioondoka", "Average membership length": "Wastani wa muda wa uanachama", "Base ↑": "Msingi ↑", "Best ↑": "Bora ↑", "Capital to open the store": "Mtaji wa kufungua duka", "Competitors can sell medicines; Afya Basics does not.": "Washindani wanaweza kuuza dawa; Afya Basics haiuzi.", "Cost to win one member": "Gharama ya kumpata mwanachama mmoja", "Cumulative cash from the store": "Fedha taslimu limbikizi kutoka dukani", "Cumulative cash of the chain · base, best and downside": "Fedha taslimu limbikizi za mtandao wa maduka · hali ya msingi, hali bora na hali ya kushuka", "Downside ↓": "Kushuka ↓", "Every store in the plan follows the same pattern. In its first year it reaches 55% of a mature store’s sales, in its second year 85%, and from its third year the full TSh 1.6B a year. Its gross profit is 26% of sales, and its running costs are TSh 315M a year, the same as the flagship, including the flagship’s prime-street rent.": "Kila duka katika mpango hufuata mtindo uleule. Katika mwaka wake wa kwanza hufikia 55% ya mauzo ya duka lililokomaa, katika mwaka wa pili 85%, na kuanzia mwaka wa tatu TSh bilioni 1.6 kamili kwa mwaka. Faida ghafi yake ni 26% ya mauzo, na gharama zake za uendeshaji ni TSh milioni 315 kwa mwaka, sawa na duka kuu, ikijumuisha kodi ya pango ya barabara kuu ya duka kuu.", "For an investor, the most important growth question is whether the money spent to win a customer comes back, and how fast. The calculation below uses only inputs from the master model and shows every step.": "Kwa mwekezaji, swali muhimu zaidi la ukuaji ni iwapo fedha zinazotumika kumpata mteja zinarudi, na kwa kasi gani. Hesabu iliyo hapa chini inatumia takwimu kutoka modeli kuu pekee na inaonyesha kila hatua.", "Gate 4 · National chain": "Kizingiti 4 · Mtandao wa kitaifa", "Goodlife multiplied its network by 7.8 in under nine years. Afya Basics plans to go from 1 to 47 stores in twelve years, a slower pace that starts from a single store and is gated at every stage. The comparison does not prove that Afya Basics will succeed; it shows that customers in the region do move from small independent outlets to an organised, trusted chain, and that investors and lenders finance that move.": "Goodlife iliongeza mtandao wake mara 7.8 ndani ya chini ya miaka tisa. Afya Basics inapanga kutoka duka 1 hadi maduka 47 ndani ya miaka kumi na mbili, kasi ndogo zaidi inayoanzia duka moja na yenye kizingiti katika kila hatua. Ulinganisho huu hauthibitishi kwamba Afya Basics itafanikiwa; unaonyesha kwamba wateja katika kanda hii kweli huhama kutoka maduka madogo huru kwenda kwenye mtandao wa maduka uliopangwa na unaoaminika, na kwamba wawekezaji na wakopeshaji hufadhili mabadiliko hayo.", "Gross profit at 26%": "Faida ghafi kwa 26%", "Gross profit on those products": "Faida ghafi kwenye bidhaa hizo", "How the money would be raised · planning outline": "Jinsi fedha zitakavyopatikana · muhtasari wa mipango", "In the base case the cumulative figure falls until year 6 and then rises, because from then on the mature stores earn more than the new openings cost. The deepest point is TSh 2.13B, of which the first TSh 263M is the flagship in year 1, covered by the seed. The capital needed after the seed is therefore about TSh 1.86B. In the best case it falls to about TSh 412M.": "Katika hali ya msingi kiasi limbikizi kinashuka hadi mwaka wa 6 kisha kinapanda, kwa sababu kuanzia hapo maduka yaliyokomaa hupata zaidi ya gharama ya kufungua maduka mapya. Kiwango cha chini kabisa ni TSh bilioni 2.13, ambapo TSh milioni 263 za kwanza ni duka kuu katika mwaka wa 1, zinazogharamiwa na mtaji wa mwanzo. Kwa hiyo mtaji unaohitajika baada ya mtaji wa mwanzo ni takriban TSh bilioni 1.86. Katika hali bora unashuka hadi takriban TSh milioni 412.", "In the downside case the money at risk is the seed, not the twelve-year capital plan. The founders would then use the levers the gates are designed to trigger: move to a lower-rent format, cut costs in line with the cost-cut triggers in section 7.3, and widen the business services in section 5.2, before asking for more capital.": "Katika hali ya kushuka, fedha zilizo hatarini ni mtaji wa mwanzo, si mpango wa mtaji wa miaka kumi na mbili. Waanzilishi wangetumia hatua ambazo vizingiti vimeundwa kuzichochea: kuhamia muundo wa duka wenye kodi ya pango ndogo zaidi, kupunguza gharama kulingana na vichochezi vya kupunguza gharama katika sehemu ya 7.3, na kupanua huduma kwa taasisi katika sehemu ya 5.2, kabla ya kuomba mtaji zaidi.", "It also names a risk. A chain like Goodlife could enter Tanzania. Afya Basics’ answer is to be different, not only earlier: Goodlife is a pharmacy chain built around medicines, while Afya Basics is built around the household’s monthly plan, the free check, the Afya Box and delivery, with medicines supplied through a licensed partner. A pharmacy chain entering Tanzania could even become a partner pharmacy rather than a rival.": "Pia unaonyesha hatari moja. Mtandao wa maduka kama Goodlife unaweza kuingia Tanzania. Jibu la Afya Basics ni kuwa tofauti, si kuwa wa kwanza tu: Goodlife ni mtandao wa maduka ya dawa uliojengwa kuzunguka dawa, wakati Afya Basics imejengwa kuzunguka mpango wa kila mwezi wa kaya, kipimo cha bure, Afya Box na usafirishaji, huku dawa zikitolewa kupitia mshirika mwenye leseni. Mtandao wa maduka ya dawa unaoingia Tanzania unaweza hata kuwa duka la dawa mshirika badala ya mshindani.", "Lifetime gross profit of a member": "Faida ghafi ya mwanachama katika kipindi chote cha uanachama", "Lifetime value ÷ cost to win": "Thamani ya maisha ya mwanachama ÷ gharama ya kumpata", "Mama na mtoto essentials": "Mahitaji muhimu ya mama na mtoto", "Marketing in year 1": "Masoko katika mwaka wa 1", "Medicines reach Afya members through a licensed partner pharmacy under a written agreement (section 4.5): the pharmacist sells and dispenses, the sealed bag travels with the box. Members get one delivery; Afya keeps its licence simple and its site choice open.": "Dawa huwafikia wanachama wa Afya kupitia duka la dawa mshirika lenye leseni chini ya makubaliano ya maandishi (sehemu ya 4.5): mfamasia huuza na kutoa dawa, mfuko uliofungwa husafirishwa pamoja na boksi. Wanachama hupata usafirishaji mmoja; Afya hudumisha leseni yake kuwa rahisi na uchaguzi wa eneo kuwa wazi.", "Months to earn back the cost": "Miezi ya kurejesha gharama", "New members in year 1": "Wanachama wapya katika mwaka wa 1", "One new store": "Duka moja jipya", "Partnerships are treated cautiously in the plan. No business revenue is counted in the first year. From year 2 it is added at 8.0% of store sales, a modest figure for a business whose products are bought every month by clinics, employers and schools. And no partner is counted as signed: each one is a target that must be won through the five-stage pipeline described below.": "Ushirikiano unashughulikiwa kwa tahadhari katika mpango. Hakuna mapato ya biashara kwa taasisi yanayohesabiwa katika mwaka wa kwanza. Kuanzia mwaka wa 2 yanaongezwa kwa 8.0% ya mauzo ya duka, kiwango cha wastani kwa biashara ambayo bidhaa zake hununuliwa kila mwezi na kliniki, waajiri na shule. Na hakuna mshirika anayehesabiwa kuwa amesaini: kila mmoja ni lengo linalopaswa kupatikana kupitia mchakato wa hatua tano ulioelezwa hapa chini.", "Products in an average box, net of VAT": "Bidhaa katika boksi la wastani, bila VAT", "Read across the table: a new store loses money in its first year, makes a small profit in its second, and from its third year earns about TSh 101M a year. It repays its opening capital and first-year loss during its fifth year of trading. Once mature, each store returns about 59% a year on the TSh 170M invested in it.": "Soma jedwali kwa mlalo: duka jipya hupata hasara katika mwaka wake wa kwanza, hupata faida ndogo katika mwaka wa pili, na kuanzia mwaka wa tatu hupata takriban TSh milioni 101 kwa mwaka. Hurejesha mtaji wake wa kufungua na hasara ya mwaka wa kwanza katika mwaka wake wa tano wa biashara. Likishakomaa, kila duka hurejesha takriban 59% kwa mwaka kwenye TSh milioni 170 zilizowekezwa ndani yake.", "Result": "Matokeo", "Sales": "Mauzo", "Scale limited to ±TSh 3B · the best case rises above it from year 8 and the downside falls below it from year 5 · before tax, interest, working capital and lease advances": "Kipimo kimewekewa kikomo cha ±TSh bilioni 3 · hali bora inapanda juu yake kuanzia mwaka wa 8 na hali ya kushuka inashuka chini yake kuanzia mwaka wa 5 · kabla ya kodi, riba, mtaji wa uendeshaji na malipo ya awali ya kodi ya pango", "Seed, TSh 340M: the flagship, released in three tranches (section 6.3). Growth round 1, at gate 1 (about year 2): stores 2 to 4 and the packing hub, about TSh 801M over years 2 and 3. Growth round 2 and development-finance debt, at gate 3 (about year 4): the national network, about TSh 1.06B over years 4 to 6. From year 7 the chain funds its own openings. Regional pharmacy chains have financed exactly this phase with private equity and loans from development-finance institutions": "Mtaji wa mwanzo, TSh milioni 340: duka kuu, unaotolewa kwa awamu tatu (sehemu ya 6.3). Awamu ya uwekezaji wa ukuaji ya 1, kwenye kizingiti cha 1 (takriban mwaka wa 2): maduka ya 2 hadi 4 na kituo cha kufungashia, takriban TSh milioni 801 katika miaka ya 2 na 3. Awamu ya uwekezaji wa ukuaji ya 2 na mikopo ya taasisi za fedha za maendeleo, kwenye kizingiti cha 3 (takriban mwaka wa 4): mtandao wa kitaifa, takriban TSh bilioni 1.06 katika miaka ya 4 hadi 6. Kuanzia mwaka wa 7 mtandao wa maduka hugharamia ufunguzi wa maduka yake yenyewe. Mitandao ya maduka ya dawa ya kikanda imefadhili hatua hii hasa kwa mitaji ya uwekezaji binafsi na mikopo kutoka taasisi za fedha za maendeleo", "Store profit before head office": "Faida ya duka kabla ya gharama za makao makuu", "TSh 1.86B base · TSh 20.1B downside": "TSh bilioni 1.86 hali ya msingi · TSh bilioni 20.1 hali ya kushuka", "TSh 15,385 × 12.5 months": "TSh 15,385 × miezi 12.5", "TSh 170M · seed TSh 340M": "TSh milioni 170 · mtaji wa mwanzo TSh milioni 340", "TSh 2.5M × 12 months + TSh 7M launch": "TSh milioni 2.5 × miezi 12 + TSh milioni 7 za uzinduzi", "Tanzania has 80.98 million mobile money accounts, 58.9 million internet subscriptions and 42.5% smartphone penetration (March 2026)": "Tanzania ina akaunti milioni 80.98 za pesa za simu, usajili wa intaneti milioni 58.9 na kiwango cha matumizi ya simu janja cha 42.5% (Machi 2026)", "Tanzania has more than 17,400 accredited drug dispensing outlets (ADDOs)": "Tanzania ina zaidi ya maduka 17,400 ya dawa muhimu yaliyoidhinishwa (ADDO)", "Tanzania · islands": "Tanzania · visiwani", "Tanzanian households already buy health products from more than 17,400 accredited drug shops, from pharmacies, supermarkets, street sellers, apps and hospital pharmacies. Each serves one need well. None plans the household’s health month by month. That is the position Afya Basics is built to hold.": "Kaya za Tanzania tayari hununua bidhaa za afya kutoka zaidi ya maduka 17,400 ya dawa yaliyoidhinishwa, kutoka maduka ya dawa, supamaketi, wachuuzi wa mitaani, programu za simu na maduka ya dawa ya hospitali. Kila moja hutimiza hitaji moja vizuri. Hakuna hata moja linalopanga afya ya kaya mwezi kwa mwezi. Hiyo ndiyo nafasi ambayo Afya Basics imejengwa kuishika.", "Tanzanian network profitable after head office": "Mtandao wa Tanzania unapata faida baada ya gharama za makao makuu", "The digital share is 30% of the monthly budget, TSh 750,000. Published Facebook advertising prices for Tanzania are not available; in neighbouring Kenya, 1,000 ad views cost between US$0.90 and US$2.40 in 2026": "Sehemu ya kidijitali ni 30% ya bajeti ya kila mwezi, TSh 750,000. Bei zilizochapishwa za matangazo ya Facebook kwa Tanzania hazipatikani; katika nchi jirani ya Kenya, mara 1,000 za kutazamwa kwa tangazo ziligharimu kati ya US$0.90 na US$2.40 mwaka 2026", "The downside scenario assumes demand 25% below plan and costs 5% above. In that case a mature store sells TSh 1.2B a year, earns TSh 312M gross profit and has running costs of TSh 331M: it loses about TSh 18.8M a year even when mature.": "Hali ya kushuka inadhani mahitaji yatakuwa 25% chini ya mpango na gharama 5% juu yake. Katika hali hiyo duka lililokomaa huuza TSh bilioni 1.2 kwa mwaka, hupata faida ghafi ya TSh milioni 312 na lina gharama za uendeshaji za TSh milioni 331: hupata hasara ya takriban TSh milioni 18.8 kwa mwaka hata likiwa limekomaa.", "The figure most worth watching after launch is the share of members who leave each month. At 8.0%, an average member stays 12.5 months. If retention practices bring it down to 6%, the average membership rises to about 16.7 months and each member’s lifetime gross profit rises by a third, with no extra marketing.": "Takwimu inayostahili kufuatiliwa zaidi baada ya kuanza ni uwiano wa wanachama wanaoondoka kila mwezi. Kwa 8.0%, mwanachama wa wastani hubaki miezi 12.5. Iwapo mbinu za kuwabakiza wanachama zitaishusha hadi 6%, wastani wa uanachama hupanda hadi takriban miezi 16.7 na faida ghafi ya kila mwanachama katika kipindi chote cha uanachama hupanda kwa theluthi moja, bila masoko ya ziada.", "The market is large but split into thousands of single small outlets": "Soko ni kubwa lakini limegawanyika katika maelfu ya maduka madogo yanayojitegemea", "The master model sets marketing at TSh 2.5M a month, TSh 30M a year, with a further TSh 7M for the launch inside the seed. That is a small budget for a new brand, and it is deliberately so: the most expensive “advertising” Afya Basics pays for is the rent of a visible site, which is already in the store’s costs. The marketing budget is spread across six channels, starting with the split shown above and moved each quarter towards the channels that bring new members most cheaply.": "Modeli kuu inaweka masoko kwa TSh milioni 2.5 kwa mwezi, TSh milioni 30 kwa mwaka, pamoja na TSh milioni 7 za ziada kwa uzinduzi ndani ya mtaji wa mwanzo. Hiyo ni bajeti ndogo kwa chapa mpya, na ni hivyo kwa makusudi: “tangazo” la gharama kubwa zaidi ambalo Afya Basics hulipia ni kodi ya pango ya eneo linaloonekana, ambayo tayari imo katika gharama za duka. Bajeti ya masoko imegawanywa katika njia sita, ikianza na mgawanyo ulioonyeshwa hapo juu na kuhamishwa kila robo mwaka kuelekea njia zinazoleta wanachama wapya kwa gharama nafuu zaidi.", "The measure that decides where money goes is not views or likes but cost per new member: marketing spent in a channel divided by the members who joined after first contact through it. Each channel is tracked because every customer’s first visit is recorded with how they heard of Afya Basics.": "Kipimo kinachoamua fedha zinaelekezwa wapi si idadi ya mara za kutazamwa au kupendwa, bali gharama kwa kila mwanachama mpya: fedha za masoko zilizotumika katika njia fulani zikigawanywa kwa wanachama waliojiunga baada ya mawasiliano yao ya kwanza kupitia njia hiyo. Kila njia hufuatiliwa kwa sababu ziara ya kwanza ya kila mteja hurekodiwa pamoja na jinsi alivyosikia kuhusu Afya Basics.", "The model calculates business revenue as 8.0% on top of what the stores sell to households. Because the published yearly revenue already includes it, the business share of a year’s revenue is the total multiplied by 8.0% and divided by 1.08.": "Modeli hukokotoa mapato ya biashara kwa taasisi kama 8.0% juu ya kile ambacho maduka huuza kwa kaya. Kwa kuwa mapato ya mwaka yaliyochapishwa tayari yanayajumuisha, sehemu ya biashara kwa taasisi katika mapato ya mwaka ni jumla ikizidishwa kwa 8.0% na kugawanywa kwa 1.08.", "The model charges every store the flagship’s rent of TSh 11.9M a month, TSh 143M a year. Most later stores will be neighbourhood stores on secondary streets. At the start-small estimate of about US$14 per m² a month, a 180 m² neighbourhood store would pay about TSh 6.7M a month. That would add about TSh 63M a year to each mature store’s profit, raising it to about TSh 164M. This saving is not in the model: it is upside, tested store by store before each lease is signed.": "Modeli inatoza kila duka kodi ya pango ya duka kuu ya TSh milioni 11.9 kwa mwezi, TSh milioni 143 kwa mwaka. Maduka mengi ya baadaye yatakuwa maduka ya mtaani kwenye barabara za pili. Kwa makadirio ya chaguo la kuanza kidogo ya takriban US$14 kwa m² kwa mwezi, duka la mtaani la 180 m² lingelipa takriban TSh milioni 6.7 kwa mwezi. Hilo lingeongeza takriban TSh milioni 63 kwa mwaka kwenye faida ya kila duka lililokomaa, na kuipandisha hadi takriban TSh milioni 164. Akiba hii haimo kwenye modeli: ni faida ya ziada, inayojaribiwa duka kwa duka kabla ya kila mkataba wa pango kusainiwa.", "The most important lever · rent": "Kichocheo muhimu zaidi · kodi ya pango", "The partner types are not equal. Schools, hotels and employers decide quickly and order on a fixed rhythm (school terms, hotel rooms, staff numbers), so they are approached first. Insurers and large clinics take longer to sign but bring larger, steadier volumes. Diaspora associations bring households that pay from abroad, often for a parent’s box. The matrix below scores each type on how soon it brings revenue, how easy it is to win and how much it is worth.": "Aina za washirika hazilingani. Shule, hoteli na waajiri huamua haraka na huagiza kwa mpangilio maalum (mihula ya shule, vyumba vya hoteli, idadi ya wafanyakazi), hivyo hufikiwa kwanza. Makampuni ya bima na kliniki kubwa huchukua muda mrefu zaidi kusaini lakini huleta kiasi kikubwa na thabiti zaidi. Jumuiya za diaspora huleta kaya zinazolipa kutoka nje ya nchi, mara nyingi kwa ajili ya boksi la mzazi. Jedwali lililo hapa chini linapima kila aina kwa jinsi inavyoleta mapato mapema, urahisi wa kuipata na thamani yake.", "The plan grows Afya Basics from one flagship in Dar es Salaam to 47 stores across Tanzania and East Africa in twelve years, reaching TSh 80B of revenue in year 12 in the base case. Every new stage opens only when the stores already open have met written targets, so investors’ capital follows evidence rather than optimism.": "Mpango unaikuza Afya Basics kutoka duka kuu moja Dar es Salaam hadi maduka 47 kote Tanzania na Afrika Mashariki ndani ya miaka kumi na mbili, na kufikia mapato ya TSh bilioni 80 katika mwaka wa 12 kwa hali ya msingi. Kila hatua mpya hufunguliwa tu pale maduka yaliyokwisha kufunguliwa yanapotimiza malengo yaliyoandikwa, hivyo mtaji wa wawekezaji hufuata ushahidi badala ya matumaini.", "The plan works in three steps. First, people are brought to the store by the store itself, a standalone store with a free Afya Check at the door, supported by WhatsApp, community health talks, radio and clinic referrals. Second, the adviser explains the reading and helps the person choose the right product, without pressure. Third, the customer’s basket is saved, a reminder arrives before the product runs out, and the natural next step is a monthly box delivered to the door.": "Mpango hufanya kazi kwa hatua tatu. Kwanza, watu huvutiwa dukani na duka lenyewe, duka lenye Afya Check ya bure mlangoni, likisaidiwa na WhatsApp, mazungumzo ya afya ya kijamii, redio na rufaa kutoka kliniki. Pili, mshauri hueleza kipimo na humsaidia mtu kuchagua bidhaa sahihi, bila shinikizo. Tatu, kikapu cha mteja huhifadhiwa, kikumbusho hufika kabla bidhaa haijaisha, na hatua inayofuata kwa kawaida ni boksi la kila mwezi linalofikishwa mlangoni.", "The strongest evidence that organised health retail can grow in East Africa comes from Kenya. Goodlife Pharmacies had 19 stores when the investor LeapFrog joined in November 2016; by July 2025 it had 148 stores in Kenya and Uganda, employed 593 full-time staff and served more than three million customers": "Ushahidi wenye nguvu zaidi kwamba rejareja ya afya iliyopangwa inaweza kukua Afrika Mashariki unatoka Kenya. Goodlife Pharmacies ilikuwa na maduka 19 wakati mwekezaji LeapFrog alipojiunga Novemba 2016; kufikia Julai 2025 ilikuwa na maduka 148 nchini Kenya na Uganda, iliajiri wafanyakazi 593 wa kudumu na ilihudumia zaidi ya wateja milioni tatu", "The twelve-year table below still shows the downside network opening 47 stores, so that the three scenarios can be compared on the same store count. In practice the gates would prevent it. Gate 1 requires the flagship to make a monthly profit for three months in a row before store 2 is funded. At downside demand the flagship would not pass that gate, the growth round would not be raised, and no second store would open.": "Jedwali la miaka kumi na mbili lililo hapa chini bado linaonyesha mtandao wa hali ya kushuka ukifungua maduka 47, ili hali hizi tatu ziweze kulinganishwa kwa idadi ileile ya maduka. Kiuhalisia vizingiti vingezuia hilo. Kizingiti cha 1 kinahitaji duka kuu kupata faida ya kila mwezi kwa miezi mitatu mfululizo kabla duka la 2 halijafadhiliwa. Kwa mahitaji ya hali ya kushuka duka kuu lisingevuka kizingiti hicho, awamu ya uwekezaji wa ukuaji isingekusanywa, na hakuna duka la pili lingefunguliwa.", "These figures exclude corporate tax, interest, working capital and the lease advance of each new store, so the real requirement will be somewhat higher. They will be refined in each round’s financial model.": "Takwimu hizi hazijumuishi kodi ya kampuni, riba, mtaji wa uendeshaji na malipo ya awali ya kodi ya pango ya kila duka jipya, hivyo hitaji halisi litakuwa juu kidogo. Zitaboreshwa katika modeli ya kifedha ya kila awamu ya uwekezaji.", "This section compares Afya Basics with five types of outlet, shows the position no one holds, explains the moments when households switch, and sets out the advantages that become harder to copy as the network grows.": "Sehemu hii inailinganisha Afya Basics na aina tano za maduka, inaonyesha nafasi ambayo hakuna anayeishika, inaeleza nyakati ambapo kaya hubadilisha mahali pa kununua, na inaweka wazi faida ambazo zinakuwa ngumu zaidi kuigwa kadiri mtandao unavyokua.", "This section explains each channel and what it costs, shows what the customer actually sees, sets out the first-year calendar and the campaigns, and ends with the numbers that matter to an investor: what it costs to win one member, how quickly that money comes back, and how much a member is worth over their membership.": "Sehemu hii inaeleza kila njia ya masoko na gharama yake, inaonyesha kile ambacho mteja anakiona hasa, inaweka kalenda ya mwaka wa kwanza na kampeni, na inahitimisha kwa takwimu muhimu kwa mwekezaji: gharama ya kumpata mwanachama mmoja, jinsi fedha hizo zinavyorudi haraka, na thamani ya mwanachama katika kipindi chote cha uanachama wake.", "Three points make these figures conservative. First, the whole marketing budget is charged to members, although the same spending also brings in every walk-in customer and online order. Second, the 26% margin on box products is lower than the 32% earned on store sales, because members pay less. Third, the packing box and delivery are charged at cost, so they add no profit here. A ratio of lifetime value to acquisition cost above 3 is generally read as healthy; the model gives about 4.3.": "Mambo matatu yanazifanya takwimu hizi kuwa za tahadhari. Kwanza, bajeti yote ya masoko inatozwa kwa wanachama, ingawa matumizi hayohayo pia huleta kila mteja wa kupita na kila oda ya mtandaoni. Pili, faida ya 26% kwenye bidhaa za boksi ni ndogo kuliko 32% inayopatikana kwenye mauzo ya dukani, kwa sababu wanachama hulipa kidogo. Tatu, boksi la kufungashia na usafirishaji vinatozwa kwa gharama halisi, hivyo haviongezi faida hapa. Uwiano wa thamani ya maisha ya mwanachama kwa gharama ya kumpata unaozidi 3 kwa kawaida huchukuliwa kuwa mzuri; modeli inatoa takriban 4.3.", "Three questions decide whether the plan is credible, and this section answers each with the numbers. Does one store make money once it is mature? How much capital does the chain need, and where does it come from? And what happens if customers buy less than planned? The answers are: yes, about TSh 101M a year before head office; about TSh 1.86B beyond the seed, raised in two later rounds and with development-finance debt; and if demand is lower, the gates stop the expansion so the loss is limited to what has already been invested.": "Maswali matatu huamua iwapo mpango unaaminika, na sehemu hii inajibu kila moja kwa takwimu. Je, duka moja hupata faida likishakomaa? Mtandao wa maduka unahitaji mtaji kiasi gani, na utatoka wapi? Na nini kitatokea iwapo wateja watanunua kidogo kuliko ilivyopangwa? Majibu ni: ndiyo, takriban TSh milioni 101 kwa mwaka kabla ya gharama za makao makuu; takriban TSh bilioni 1.86 zaidi ya mtaji wa mwanzo, zitakazopatikana katika awamu mbili za baadaye pamoja na mikopo ya taasisi za fedha za maendeleo; na iwapo mahitaji yatakuwa madogo, vizingiti husimamisha upanuzi ili hasara iishie kwenye kile ambacho tayari kimewekezwa.", "Today · a small shop, gaps on the shelves, no record of the household": "Leo · duka dogo, mapengo kwenye rafu, hakuna kumbukumbu ya kaya", "Total revenue in year 5 is TSh 15.2B across 10 stores. Business revenue is TSh 15.2B × 0.08 ÷ 1.08 = TSh 1.13B. At an average box of TSh 80,500, that equals about 1,165 staff or patient boxes a month across the network, or roughly 117 per store. A single employer with 80 staff on the Afya Kazini service, or one maternity ward referring new mothers, would supply a large part of one store’s share.": "Jumla ya mapato katika mwaka wa 5 ni TSh bilioni 15.2 kwa maduka 10. Mapato ya biashara kwa taasisi ni TSh bilioni 15.2 × 0.08 ÷ 1.08 = TSh bilioni 1.13. Kwa boksi la wastani la TSh 80,500, hiyo ni sawa na takriban maboksi 1,165 ya wafanyakazi au wagonjwa kwa mwezi katika mtandao mzima, au takriban 117 kwa kila duka. Mwajiri mmoja mwenye wafanyakazi 80 kwenye huduma ya Afya Kazini, au wodi moja ya wazazi inayoleta akina mama wapya kwa rufaa, angetosheleza sehemu kubwa ya mgao wa duka moja.", "Two changes in Tanzania make partners more valuable now than a few years ago. The Universal Health Insurance Act requires every resident to have at least basic cover and every employer to ensure its staff are insured": "Mabadiliko mawili nchini Tanzania yanawafanya washirika kuwa na thamani kubwa zaidi sasa kuliko miaka michache iliyopita. Sheria ya Bima ya Afya kwa Wote inamtaka kila mkazi kuwa na angalau bima ya msingi na kila mwajiri kuhakikisha wafanyakazi wake wana bima", "Two rules protect the business. No partner may exceed about one-fifth of business revenue, so the loss of one client cannot damage the network. And partners pay the same published price as households: what they gain is reliability, one invoice and delivery on a fixed day, not hidden discounts the customer-funded model could not carry.": "Kanuni mbili hulinda biashara. Hakuna mshirika anayeruhusiwa kuzidi takriban moja ya tano ya mapato ya biashara kwa taasisi, hivyo kumpoteza mteja mmoja hakuwezi kuudhuru mtandao. Na washirika hulipa bei ileile iliyotangazwa kama kaya: wanachopata ni uhakika, ankara moja na usafirishaji kwa siku maalum, si punguzo lililofichwa ambalo modeli inayofadhiliwa na wateja isingeweza kulibeba.", "What that means for an investor": "Maana yake kwa mwekezaji", "What the comparison shows": "Ulinganisho unaonyesha nini", "WhatsApp & digital ·": "WhatsApp na kidijitali ·", "WhatsApp or social platforms change their rules or prices.": "WhatsApp au mitandao ya kijamii inabadilisha kanuni au bei zake.", "Worked example · one month of WhatsApp and digital advertising": "Mfano wa hesabu · mwezi mmoja wa matangazo ya WhatsApp na ya kidijitali", "Worked example · year 5, base case": "Mfano wa hesabu · mwaka wa 5, hali ya msingi", "Year 3 and after": "Mwaka wa 3 na kuendelea", "Your Afya Check today: BP": "Kipimo chako cha Afya Check leo: BP", "agreements signed today: every partner is a target": "makubaliano yaliyosainiwa leo: kila mshirika ni lengo", "business sales added on top of store sales in the model, from year 2": "mauzo kwa taasisi yanayoongezwa juu ya mauzo ya dukani katika modeli, kuanzia mwaka wa 2", "business sales counted in year 1, so the first store must prove itself on households alone": "mauzo kwa taasisi yanayohesabiwa katika mwaka wa 1, hivyo duka la kwanza lazima lijithibitishe kwa kaya pekee", "business sales in year 12, base case": "mauzo kwa taasisi katika mwaka wa 12, hali ya msingi", "business sales in year 2, base case": "mauzo kwa taasisi katika mwaka wa 2, hali ya msingi", "capital to open each new store": "mtaji wa kufungua kila duka jipya", "deepest point · year 6": "kiwango cha chini kabisa · mwaka wa 6", "first year the whole chain is profitable before interest and tax (EBITDA)": "mwaka wa kwanza ambapo mtandao mzima wa maduka unapata faida kabla ya riba na kodi (EBITDA)", "for a mature store’s yearly profit to repay its opening capital": "kwa faida ya mwaka ya duka lililokomaa kurejesha mtaji wake wa kufungua", "gross profit a member brings each month, after VAT and payment fees": "faida ghafi ambayo mwanachama huleta kila mwezi, baada ya VAT na ada za malipo", "lifetime gross profit of a member compared with the cost of winning them": "faida ghafi ya mwanachama katika kipindi chote cha uanachama ikilinganishwa na gharama ya kumpata", "marketing a month, plus TSh 7M launch budget in the seed": "masoko kwa mwezi, pamoja na bajeti ya uzinduzi ya TSh milioni 7 ndani ya mtaji wa mwanzo", "marketing spent per new member in year 1": "fedha za masoko zilizotumika kwa kila mwanachama mpya katika mwaka wa 1", "outside capital the chain needs after the seed, base case": "mtaji wa nje unaohitajika na mtandao wa maduka baada ya mtaji wa mwanzo, hali ya msingi", "partner types targeted: clinics, insurers, employers, schools, hotels, diaspora groups": "aina za washirika zinazolengwa: kliniki, makampuni ya bima, waajiri, shule, hoteli, jumuiya za diaspora", "revenue in year 12, base case": "mapato katika mwaka wa 12, hali ya msingi", "stores by year 12, opened in 8 gated stages": "maduka kufikia mwaka wa 12, yanayofunguliwa katika hatua 8 zenye vizingiti", "to earn back the marketing spent on one member": "kurejesha fedha za masoko zilizotumika kwa mwanachama mmoja", "today · the shelf is empty again": "leo · rafu iko tupu tena", "unlocks: All major Tanzanian cities": "hufungua: Miji yote mikubwa ya Tanzania", "unlocks: Nairobi & Kampala pilots": "hufungua: Majaribio ya Nairobi na Kampala", "unlocks: Open Arusha & Dodoma": "hufungua: Kufungua Arusha na Dodoma", "unlocks: Open store 2 + packing hub": "hufungua: Kufungua duka la 2 + kituo cha kufungashia", "where a partner is welcomed": "mahali ambapo mshirika hukaribishwa", "where every campaign starts": "mahali ambapo kila kampeni huanzia", "× 26% margin, less 1.2% mobile-money fees on the whole box": "× faida ya 26%, ukitoa ada za pesa za simu za 1.2% kwenye boksi zima"});
